      "makingsoundmachines/mpe_test": {
        "Author": "makingsoundmachines",
        "Date": "2026-11-19",
        "Tags": "midi",
        "name": "MPE Surface",
        "description": "A configurable MPE play surface for Plinky 12, based on mmalex's MPE Test. Two play surfaces (A and B), each with a dedicated brightness (CC74) slider mapped to Plinky's sample-start / wavetable-position parameter. It accepts normal MIDI on channels 1 and 16 for the two sounds, as well as MPE for up to two zones, supporting per-note pitch bend, brightness, and pressure. It also sends data in MPE format. The mode pads below the play surfaces open the usual synth edit and preset load/save pages, using the same parameter order as Toadstep and Blocks. Click the right-up button for the settings pages: root note, scale, string stride (semitones between strings; snapped to the scale on a scale surface, exact on a chromatic one), surface (scale: every pad is a scale note; chromatic: every pad is a semitone and only scale notes are lit), string direction, how the surface is split between A and B, start (root: the lowest string starts on the root; fix: it starts on the scale note nearest C1, or on C1 itself on a chromatic surface), and glide. Settings are saved with the song.",
