      "perplex_on/arcade_12": {
        "Author": "PERPLEX ON",
        "Preferred Panels": "blocks",
        "Tags": "game, stack, breakout, generative, sequencer, sonification, midi",
        "name": "ARCADE12",
        "description": "Two games that write their own soundtrack, one cartridge slot. SELECTOR: both games run as silent demos, SELECT GAME rolls between them. Tap the left demo for KLOTZ, the right one for PRALL (an arcade start jingle plays). The lettering is not a button. Bottom-right pad in a game: tap = play / pause, hold 0.7 s = back to the selector. A run in progress waits there, paused. KLOTZ (falling blocks): swipe left / right moves the stone, swipe down drops it on the next 16th, tap rotates. The stack is a 10-step sequencer against the 16-step bar, landing strums a chord, cleared lines move the harmony, four lines at once modulate up a fourth. One extra layer per level. PRALL (breakout on the clock): drag moves the paddle, tap or swipe up launches. Every bounce is a note: brick row = height in the chord, brick column = which chord tone. Cleared rows move the chords, every level is a song. Power-ups: HALF, DOUBLE, MULTI, WIDE. Each game keeps its own voices, mix, MIDI channels, root, scale, settings. HIGH SCORES: top 5 per game, stored with the panel settings. After game over the score scrolls across the grid; a new best plays a fanfare. Pages: Play / Sound (current game, bottom row selects + auditions) / Save-Load (both sound sets). Settings (right-up): the current game's.",
        "_library_kind": "community",
        "_cpp": "COMMUNITY_PANELS/perplex_on/arcade_12/arcade_12.cpp",
